Evaluate selected DAG artifacts and return their values. This executes project code and may run warehouse queries, so it is not read-only. Artifacts are evaluated independently: one failure does not discard the others' results.

Evaluation reuses cached results by default and computes missing dependencies automatically. Set `rerun: true` when the user requests a refresh or the underlying source data may have changed. This refreshes the selected artifacts before evaluating them. Cached upstream inputs may still be reused; explicitly include upstream source artifacts when their data needs refreshing too. Refresh invalidates downstream artifacts, but this call waits only for the artifacts you list to finish evaluating. The refresh changes shared project-ref state and affects other consumers.

Discover canonical artifact names with list_code_project_artifacts. If a source save reported reloadError, fix it before evaluating. Inspect each artifact's error, totalRows, totalItems, and truncated fields. Long errors include an explicit truncation marker. Tables return the first rows; lists and objects remain wrapped in the value column but include only their first items or keys in existing order. Full counts are included when available. To inspect omitted data, evaluate a filtered or aggregated artifact; reduce columns or large values if a preview exceeds the byte limit.

```ts
