Build a code project's app and publish a new version. Publish only when the user asks to publish or says the app is ready to share. Creating, editing, building, and previewing an app do not authorize publication. Verify relevant calculations and rendered output before publishing by default. Defer checks only for an explicit speed-first or disposable-demo request that accepts that tradeoff, and report the deferred checks. Without publication authorization, return the editor or draft preview link. Never present a draft preview as published access. Publication creates a Hex app version; it does not establish public access, reader-specific warehouse credentials, or compatibility with an external artifact. Describe who can open the app and whose credentials execute queries only when verified from the applicable app and connection settings. A successful build establishes compilation, not data or visual correctness. For static HTML hosting, read back the uploaded source and compare it with the intended content, then inspect the rendered result; do not invent SQL or DAG work. For data-backed apps, also evaluate relevant artifacts to check calculations. Use get_code_project_screenshot for the preview and get_code_project_console to investigate runtime errors. Inspect the rendered image for correct content, readable labels, missing data, clipping, and overlaps; obtaining a screenshot alone is not verification. Initial-render capture does not test interactions; test changed controls when browser interaction is available. Reuse successful checks while relevant source and data remain unchanged; repeat affected checks after changes or unresolved failures. Report only checks actually performed. Build changed app source with check_code_project_app before inspecting its preview, passing appDirectory when it is not the default app. Reuse a successful build of unchanged source, including builds from chart or scaffold tools; extra build/check calls need a verification or recovery purpose. Publication builds again; it does not reuse an immutable verified build. That rebuild does not replace pre-publication preview verification. Parallelize independent checks where supported, after their required saves, reloads, and builds complete; by default, wait for relevant verification before publishing.

